// A C symbol declared with an integer parameter is called with an integer.
//
// `abs` is also the name of a math builtin, and the builtin used to win the name
// resolution even when the program had declared the C function: the call was typed
// as `f64` and lowering then had an i64 argument for an f64 parameter. A
// declaration is the stronger statement, so it is the one that is used, and the
// builtin stays reachable as `math.abs`.
extern int function abs(int value);

int function main() {
    var x = -9;
    print(abs(-7));
    print(abs(x));
    return 0;
}
